From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] render: repaint every output after recreating the renderer

recreate_renderer() swaps in a new wlr_renderer and allocator after a GPU
reset and re-inits render on every output, but never marks any of them
damaged. Nothing in the tree repaints an output that has not been damaged, so
after a reset the screen keeps whatever the dead renderer last left in the
framebuffer, and only regions that some client happens to damage on its own
are ever redrawn.

The result is a compositor that is technically alive and visibly wrong.
Measured on a Pixel 2 XL (msm8998, Adreno 540, mainline 6.18), where the A540
faults under load and the msm driver resets it several times a session: after
a reset the app grid stays on screen underneath everything, the notification
shade draws over it without ever clearing it so the icons show through, and
windows that were closed before the reset remain ghosted on top. Applications
that animate -- a browser, say -- come back on their own, because they damage
themselves; static layer-surfaces such as the panel and the on-screen keyboard
never do, and stay stale until something else forces a full repaint.

Damage each output as it is re-inited. phoc_output_damage_whole() is the
existing helper for exactly this, and desktop.c already uses the same
wl_list_for_each + phoc_output_damage_whole pattern after a layout change for
the same reason.

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 src/render.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/render.c b/src/render.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/render.c
+++ b/src/render.c
@@ -137,8 +137,12 @@ recreate_renderer (void *data)
   wlr_compositor = phoc_server_get_compositor (server);
   wlr_compositor_set_renderer (wlr_compositor, wlr_renderer);

-  wl_list_for_each (output, &desktop->outputs, link)
+  wl_list_for_each (output, &desktop->outputs, link) {
     wlr_output_init_render (output->wlr_output, self->wlr_allocator, self->wlr_renderer);
+    /* The old renderer's contents are gone, so nothing on screen is valid any
+     * more. Without this only self-damaging clients ever repaint. */
+    phoc_output_damage_whole (output);
+  }

   wlr_allocator_destroy (old_wlr_allocator);
   wlr_renderer_destroy (old_wlr_renderer);
--
2.51.0
